# SPDX-License-Identifier: MPL-2.0
# Mustfile (A2ML Canonical)

@abstract:
Physical State contract for JuliaPackageSpitter.jl.
Declares what must be true about this project's files and configuration.
@end

@requires:
- section: Checks
@end

## Checks

### license-present
- description: LICENSE file must exist
- run: test -f LICENSE
- severity: critical

### readme-present
- description: README must exist
- run: test -f README.adoc || test -f README.md
- severity: critical

### spdx-headers
# Retargeted at the languages this repository actually contains.
#
# The previous predicate searched for '*.rs', '*.res' and '*.gleam'. A census of
# this checkout finds ZERO files with those extensions, so `xargs -r` never ran,
# `wc -l` returned 0, and the check reported success without examining a single
# file. A gate that cannot fail is worse than no gate: it was reported green in
# every CI run since it was added while asserting nothing.
#
# The replacement covers every source extension present here — .jl (6 files),
# .agda (17), .sh (10), .ncl (7), 40 in total, all of which already carry an
# SPDX-License-Identifier — so this is a real check that passes today rather than
# a new source of red.
#
# The leading `test … -gt 0` guard is deliberate and is the part that makes this
# fail-closed: without it, deleting every source file would make the predicate
# vacuously true again, reintroducing exactly the failure mode being fixed here.
# The `head -20` truncation in the old command is also gone; it silently limited
# the audit to the first twenty files find happened to emit.
- description: Source files should have SPDX license headers
- run: test "$(find . -path ./.git -prune -o \( -name '*.jl' -o -name '*.agda' -o -name '*.sh' -o -name '*.ncl' \) -print | wc -l)" -gt 0 && find . -path ./.git -prune -o \( -name '*.jl' -o -name '*.agda' -o -name '*.sh' -o -name '*.ncl' \) -print | xargs -r grep -L 'SPDX-License-Identifier' | wc -l | grep -q '^0$'
- severity: warning

### no-banned-files
- description: No Dockerfiles or Makefiles
- run: test ! -f Dockerfile && test ! -f Makefile
- severity: critical
